{
 "plan": {
  "title": "Kids Improvement Dashboard",
  "subtitle": "How children progressed from baseline to endline by location and coach",
  "panels": [
   {
    "id": "p1",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Total kids improved",
    "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM (SELECT \"Child ID\" FROM \"baseline\" INTERSECT SELECT \"Child ID\" FROM \"endline\")",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p2",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Average shuttle run improvement by location",
    "sql": "SELECT \"Location\", AVG(\"end_shuttle\" - \"base_shuttle\") AS avg_improvement FROM (SELECT b.\"Location\", b.\"Shuttle run sec\" AS base_shuttle, e.\"Shuttle run sec\" AS end_shuttle FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e USING (\"Child ID\")) GROUP BY \"Location\" ORDER BY avg_improvement DESC LIMIT 20",
    "x": "Location",
    "y": [
     "avg_improvement"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p3",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Average sit\u2011ups improvement by coach",
    "sql": "SELECT \"Coach\", AVG(\"end_sit\" - \"base_sit\") AS avg_improvement FROM (SELECT b.\"Coach\", b.\"Sit ups\" AS base_sit, e.\"Sit ups\" AS end_sit FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e USING (\"Child ID\")) GROUP BY \"Coach\" ORDER BY avg_improvement DESC LIMIT 20",
    "x": "Coach",
    "y": [
     "avg_improvement"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p4",
    "kind": "table",
    "title": "Top 10 kids with greatest shuttle run gain",
    "sql": "SELECT b.\"Child ID\", b.\"Child name\", b.\"Location\", b.\"Coach\", b.\"Shuttle run sec\" AS base_shuttle, e.\"Shuttle run sec\" AS end_shuttle, (e.\"Shuttle run sec\" - b.\"Shuttle run sec\") AS shuttle_gain FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e USING (\"Child ID\") ORDER BY shuttle_gain DESC LIMIT 10"
   }
  ],
  "narrative": "The dashboard shows that {{p1.n}} children participated in both baseline and endline assessments. Across locations, the average improvement in shuttle run time is highest in {{p2.x}} with an average gain of {{p2.avg_improvement}} seconds. Coaches with the most effective progress are highlighted in {{p3.x}}, where the average sit\u2011up increase is {{p3.avg_improvement}} reps. The table lists the top 10 children who achieved the greatest shuttle run improvement, illustrating individual success stories."
 },
